# Cloudflare Pages — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Every public route (/, /blog, /blog/:slug) is its own real prerendered
# static file (see scripts/prerender.mjs) — no SPA fallback needed there, so
# a nonexistent URL correctly 404s (see public/404.html) instead of silently
# serving the homepage.
#
# /admin is a client-side-routed SPA section (gated by Cloudflare Access,
# never prerendered) — it needs the fallback so any /admin/* sub-path is
# served the same bundle and handled by the router. Points at a flat,
# non-"index.html" shell file (dist/admin-shell.html, written by
# scripts/prerender.mjs) rather than anything nested under /admin/ itself —
# Cloudflare auto-canonicalizes index.html/directory-index URLs, and a
# rewrite target whose own canonical form still matches the wildcard it's
# serving gets flagged as a redirect loop and silently dropped (confirmed
# via `wrangler pages dev` with dist/index.html and dist/admin/index.html
# both rejected before landing on this).
/admin    /admin-shell.html   200
/admin/*  /admin-shell.html   200
